# Build artefacts. All of this is regenerated by `npm run desktop:stage` and
# `cargo tauri build`, and together it is several gigabytes — none of it belongs
# in a repository.

# Rust build output (~7 GB with incremental artefacts).
src-tauri/target/

# Staged Next output, compiled services, and copied resources (~130 MB).
staging/

# Downloaded Node runtimes, verified against desktop/node-runtime.json (~50 MB).
.cache/

# The bundled Node binary, staged per target triple (~110 MB each).
# stage-node-runtime.mjs downloads and checksum-verifies it on demand.
src-tauri/binaries/

# Generated by tauri-build at compile time.
src-tauri/gen/

# Never commit the updater private key. The public half lives in
# tauri.conf.json; the private half belongs in a release secret and an offline
# backup, because losing it permanently strands every installed client.
*.key
!*.key.pub

# Cargo.lock DOES belong in the repo, and the root .gitignore's blanket `*.lock`
# would otherwise drop it. This is a binary crate that gets signed and shipped:
# without the lockfile, CI resolves dependency versions afresh on every release
# and "reproducible build" becomes a phrase rather than a property.
!src-tauri/Cargo.lock
